1. Token Budget Allocations (Resolved from previous global max_new_tokens=32):
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- single_niah:
    max_new_tokens: 32
    Rationale: Single passkey/needle retrieval. 32 tokens sufficient.
    
- multi_niah:
    max_new_tokens: 96
    Rationale: Three distinct needles/passkeys plus formatting to retrieve.
    At 32 tokens, dense baseline was truncated mid-answer (C_dense dropped to 33-66%).
    At 96 tokens, C_dense recovered to 100.0% (3/3) across 2K to 32K.

- ruler_kv:
    max_new_tokens: 32
    Rationale: Single key-value string lookup. 32 tokens sufficient.

- multihop_qa:
    max_new_tokens: 128
    Rationale: Multi-document synthesis where model cites context before entity name.
    At 32 tokens, dense spent its budget citing documents and lost anchors.
    At 128 tokens, dense anchor C_dense recovered to 100.0% (3/3) across 2K-16K.

- ruler_variable_tracking:
    max_new_tokens: 256
    Rationale: Requires sequential variable assignment resolution (A=1, B=A...).
    Evaluated with 256 tokens on Qwen2.5-7B: dense baseline still scored 0.0% across
    all context lengths (2K-32K). This confirms true model algorithmic incapacity /
    prompting format mismatch for Qwen2.5-7B, rather than token truncation.

2. Naming Standardizations:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- kv_quant -> kivi_style_kv_quant (or kv_quant_kivi)
    Rationale: The implementation is an asymmetric min-max grouped quantizer with
    per-channel keys and per-token values (following KIVI grouping), not the
    original published KVQuant algorithm.

